{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-from-epsilon","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-from-epsilon","kind":"definition","title":"The substrate parameter $q$ as $1 + \\varepsilon$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-epsilon"],"tags":["substrate-parameter","surreal","categorical-primitive","q-expansion","classical-limit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QFromEpsilon","text":"q-from-epsilon.md","leanSource":"q-from-epsilon.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-from-epsilon\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon \\in \\mathrm{Der}(A)</code> be the <a href=\"#def:reeb-epsilon\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">Reeb infinitesimal</a>. The <strong>substrate parameter associated to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon</code></strong> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">q := 1 + \\varepsilon,</code></pre>\n<p>interpreted inside the ordered field generated by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/q-from-epsilon.md","heading":"Definition","number":"21.4.18","page":"b/def-q-from-epsilon","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BringsSurface.QFromEpsilon","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/q-from-epsilon.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
